  "summary": "The 2010s Summer Nostalgia aesthetic is a style that romanticizes the cultural mood and imagery of summer experiences during the 2010s, especially between 2013 and 2018.",
  "description": "The 2010s Summer Nostalgia aesthetic is a style that romanticizes the cultural mood and imagery of summer experiences during the 2010s, especially between 2013 and 2018. [ 1 ] The aesthetic is inherently tied to early social media culture, particularly the peak of Tumblr and the rise of Instagram, which is often perceived as an era of care-free illusion, youthful freedom, and collective happiness. [ 1 ] The aesthetic is characterized by a photographic treatment that captures a sense of sun-bleached optimism and vivid saturation.\n\nThe summer of 2016 is often cited as the most romanticized year within this aesthetic, frequently referenced in online culture as having \"immaculate vibes,\" despite a notable degree of revisionist history applied to the era. [ 2 ]",
  "culturalContext": "Key values (per the Aesthetics Wiki): Care-free illusion, peace and joy, instant celebrity, youthful freedom, sun worship",
